WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.100
«Le Havre, Brest, Saint-Malo».

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:07.250
In 1944, towns like these
lie largely destroyed.

3
00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:10.550
Bridges, railways and ports are cut.

4
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.870
France must also judge those
accused of collaboration:

5
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:20.770
«l'épuration». Without trial, historians
estimate 9,000 to 10,000 people were killed.

6
00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:25.270
Rationing lasts until 1949.

7
00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:32.960
Yet from 1946, over 800,000
babies are born each year.

8
00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:33.700
Free, but in ruins.

9
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.000
How did France judge, rebuild
and change in just six years?

10
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:44.560
In this mission, you'll build
a timeline from 1944 to 1950,

11
00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.680
starting with «le Débarquement».

12
00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:47.990
Then you'll argue both sides:

13
00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.970
was «l'épuration» justice, or revenge?

14
00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.410
Your mission: find out what France judged,

15
00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:55.800
rebuilt and changed, and
what still lasts today.
